  "title": "The Staircase That Unpacks Itself",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "block-world chain reactions",
  "premise": "A cubic traveler needs to reach a platform, but the staircase is stored as a compact accordion tower. Pulling a clearly marked top tab releases sequential hinges, and each unfolding tread frees the next until a walkable stair reaches the platform; the final step unfolds into a welcome mat.",
  "hook": "The stairs are still in their box.",
  "visible_action": "Top tab slides; hinged block pairs rotate in sequence; treads land on supports; last panel flips into a mat.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Sequenced dependencies can make a compact object deploy in order.",
  "gate": "Fictional low-force hinges; no engineering claim about real load-bearing stairs.",
